Q.1-> Why use ONE ObjectPooler for bullets/enemies/smoke
Core answer (one sentence):
One central ObjectPooler gives a single place to create, reuse, and manage pooled objects so your game uses less memory, has fewer bugs, and is easier to control and tune.
Note:-
We use a single ObjectPooler because it gives one central place to create, reuse, and manage all pooled objects for bullets, enemies, and effects


